// A case takes literals only: a number, a string, a negated number, or a list
// of those. Anything else -- a variable, a call, arithmetic -- is rejected here
// rather than when the harness is emitted, where the diagnostic would be about
// a name that is not in scope. idc.py's wording, word for word.
//
// A list is not checked here: it is read element by element as a tuple is
// (case/given/elem/more/list.id), so each element is held to this on its own.

check_lit(int e) {
  if(is_lit(e) == 0) {
    string cur_file_v = cur_file();
    int ln = (import nline)[e];
    syn_err_tail(cur_file_v, ln, "a test case takes literals only (a number, a string, a list of those, or a struct written as P(1, 2))");
  }
} return void;
given lit_fix (0):() then prints:("")
given lit_fix (1):() then prints:("<stdin>:0: error: a test case takes literals only (a number, a string, a list of those, or a struct written as P(1, 2))\n")

is_lit(int e) {
  int r = leaf_lit(e);
  if((import nkind)[e] == "un") {
    r = neg_lit(e);
  }
} return int r;
given lit_fix (0):(1)
given lit_fix (1):(0)
